{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-made mapping from this tool's native check ids to SEI CERT C rule ids",
    "and CWE ids. It is DATA, not derived: every entry is a judgement about",
    "what defect the check reports, made by reading the check's documentation,",
    "and the harness records this file's sha256 into every run so a table can",
    "say which version of the judgement it used. A check with no entry is",
    "reported as `unmapped` -- counted, never dropped -- so the mapping's",
    "coverage is itself a number a reader can see. `cert: []` means the check",
    "names a defect CERT C has no rule for; `cwe: []` likewise.",
    "Add entries with a `note` saying why; change one only with a note saying",
    "what was wrong."
  ],
  "source": "hand-made",
  "unmapped_policy": "counted",
  "tool": "cppcheck",
